      "id": 8216,
      "name": "Silverleaf",
      "username": "Silverleaf",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-16T05:42:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I played my first ever game of Fiasco (<a href=\"http://www.bullypulpitgames.com/games/fiasco/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.bullypulpitgames.com/games/fiasco/</a>) earlier with Trent and Niel over Google Hangouts, which was awesome! We had great fun and created a pretty cool story too. Fiasco's a storytelling game which, according to the website, is&nbsp; about \"cinematic tales of small time capers gone disastrously wrong – inspired by films like <em>Blood Simple, Fargo, The Way of the Gun, Burn After Reading</em>, and <em>A Simple Plan</em>.\"</p><p>There are loads of \"playsets\" available which are basically the seting, so you can play anything from a teen romantic comedy to Renaissance Italy to a Guy Ritchie movie to a sci-fi set on an abandoned spacestation, and of course superheroes!</p><p>So, anyone interested in playing? Just gaugeing interest at the moment really.</p>",
