      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I played my first ever game of Fiasco (<a href=\"http://www.bullypulpitgames.com/games/fiasco/\">http://www.bullypulpitgames.com/games/fiasco/</a>) earlier with Trent and Niel over Google Hangouts, which was awesome! We had great fun and created a pretty cool story too. Fiasco&#39;s a storytelling game which, according to the website, is&nbsp; about &quot;cinematic tales of small time capers gone disastrously wrong &ndash; inspired by films like <em>Blood Simple, Fargo, The Way of the Gun, Burn After Reading</em>, and <em>A Simple Plan</em>.&quot;</p><p>There are loads of &quot;playsets&quot; available which are basically the seting, so you can play anything from a teen romantic comedy to Renaissance Italy to a Guy Ritchie movie to a sci-fi set on an abandoned spacestation, and of course superheroes!</p><p>So, anyone interested in playing? Just gaugeing interest at the moment really.</p>",
